WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.920
[Brady] What is the most dangerous chemical you've ever handled?

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.100
The most dangerous chemical, I believe,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:13.640
was one called cyclopentadienyl nickel nitrosyl.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.420
It was claimed at the time to be one of the most poisonous chemicals in the world.

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:22.340
It's a blood red coloured liquid - it looks pretty evil.

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.380
And I dropped the bottle on the floor, and it broke.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.860
But fortunately only the neck of the bottle broke,

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.380
so I could pick it up, and none came out.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:39.820
The molecule, or the material I've had to handle with the most care, let's say,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.940
is probably tertiary Butyllithium.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:47.420
And, I used this as a PhD student,

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.360
and it's a fantastic reagent,

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.220
we use it as a strong base when we're doing synthetic chemistry.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.240
But, if you take a concentrated solution of tertiary Butyllithium,

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.520
in a syringe and you squirt it,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.040
it bursts into flames instantaneously when it hits the atmosphere.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:07.160
I suppose it's similar to many other things that Steve has shown us on some of his videos,

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:08.980
like the Zinc chemistry.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.960
Tertiary Butyllithium, actually, is one of the most -

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:16.640
one of the molecules that I have the utmost respect for.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:22.640
Probably the most dangerous situation that I've found myself in whilst handling compounds

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.280
is when I had an ampoule,

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.080
- so an ampoule for those of you who don't know,

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.100
is a bottle which is completely sealed.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:33.580
That's all glass, and you have to break it with a hammer to get to the contents.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:38.980
and I had a 250ml bottle of SO_3,

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:43.260
and I needed to pour this into a vial which we could open and close,

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.500
or a bottle we could open and close.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.380
So I got my hammer, I'd pre-scored the glass,

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:50.840
and - I don't have an ampoule here today but -

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.180
you can imagine a sort of - a bottle,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.480
and then it goes up to a neck,

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.160
and you get a thin piece at the top,

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.120
and you hit that off with a hammer.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:02.700
So I did this, I'd three pairs of gloves on,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.080
two lab coats, and this was all wrapped round.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.120
We were in a very good fume hood

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:10.460
with scrubbers and all the rest of it.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:16.380
I hit this off, and immediately, as soon as SO_3 hits water in the air,

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.060
you get sulfuric acid.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.340
And there were just clouds and clouds of sulfuric acid.

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.960
And there I was pouring this stuff in to the glass bottle,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.860
as quick as I could.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.300
Put the top on.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.140
It was like "Wow, thank goodness for that."

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:32.760
And the - I'd three pairs of very thick gloves on,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:36.360
The outer one, it completely dissolved.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.200
It was black.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.200
The second one,

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.740
was pretty black as well.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:46.260
Luckily, the third one was intact, we were okay.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.720
But, yeah, that was a scary, scary time.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.180
And it was good fun. [He laughs]

